WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.056
Imagine waiting for GTA 6 in America.

00:00:04.056 --> 00:00:05.580
It's November 18.

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:07.104
You open YouTube,

00:00:07.104 --> 00:00:08.120
and suddenly,

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:11.168
people are already playing the game.

00:00:11.168 --> 00:00:12.184
Not tomorrow.

00:00:12.184 --> 00:00:14.724
Not in a few hours.

00:00:14.724 --> 00:00:15.740
Right now.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:22.577
But here's the strange part.

00:00:22.577 --> 00:00:25.899
Rockstar says GTA 6 launches on November 19.

00:00:25.899 --> 00:00:31.298
So how are people playing it while America is still on November 18?

00:00:31.298 --> 00:00:35.866
The answer is a country most gamers probably weren't thinking about.

00:00:35.866 --> 00:00:36.697
New Zealand.

00:00:36.697 --> 00:00:39.604
And this is where things get interesting.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:47.726
Rockstar has confirmed that GTA 6 will unlock at midnight on November 19 in each region.

00:00:47.726 --> 00:00:50.436
Not at one single moment worldwide.

00:00:50.436 --> 00:00:53.146
Each region reaches its own midnight,

00:00:53.146 --> 00:00:55.404
and the game becomes available.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:04.838
PlayStation has also confirmed that this rolling launch begins in New Zealand.

00:01:04.838 --> 00:01:06.646
Think about what that means.

00:01:06.646 --> 00:01:09.176
When Auckland reaches midnight on November 19,

00:01:09.176 --> 00:01:13.152
the United States is still on the morning of November 18.

00:01:13.152 --> 00:01:14.237
In New York,

00:01:14.237 --> 00:01:15.322
it's 6 AM.

00:01:15.322 --> 00:01:16.406
In Los Angeles,

00:01:16.406 --> 00:01:17.852
it's only 3 AM.

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:22.876
One country has entered launch day.

00:01:22.876 --> 00:01:26.044
Another is still waiting for it to arrive.

00:01:26.044 --> 00:01:32.380
And that creates an eighteen-hour difference between New Zealand's unlock and the normal US launch window.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:43.098
But here's the question everyone is asking.

00:01:43.098 --> 00:01:47.923
Can an American actually use this time difference to play GTA 6 early?

00:01:47.923 --> 00:01:50.892
That's where the New Zealand trick comes in.

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:01.295
On Xbox,

00:02:01.295 --> 00:02:05.270
players can change their console's location setting to New Zealand.

00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:06.860
The idea is simple.

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:10.438
If the console follows the New Zealand release region,

00:02:10.438 --> 00:02:15.208
an existing digital copy might become playable when the game unlocks there.

00:02:15.208 --> 00:02:19.580
Players have used similar region-switching methods for other staggered game launches.

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:24.693
But there is one detail you should not ignore.

00:02:24.693 --> 00:02:31.681
Rockstar and Microsoft have not officially guaranteed that this trick will work for GTA 6.

00:02:31.681 --> 00:02:36.340
So don't confuse a possible workaround with confirmed early access.

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:42.818
And PlayStation is a different story.

00:02:42.818 --> 00:02:48.227
Your PlayStation account is tied to the country selected when that account was created.

00:02:48.227 --> 00:02:55.568
You cannot simply turn an existing American PlayStation account into a New Zealand account by changing your console settings.

00:02:55.568 --> 00:03:00.204
A New Zealand-region purchase is a different situation from an American-region preorder.

00:03:00.204 --> 00:03:04.068
So the trick is not the same on both consoles.

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:08.297
Now let's look at the bigger picture.

00:03:08.297 --> 00:03:11.493
Why does New Zealand get the first opportunity?

00:03:11.493 --> 00:03:14.689
Because the launch is based on local midnight,

00:03:14.689 --> 00:03:16.287
not one worldwide countdown.

00:03:16.287 --> 00:03:20.682
New Zealand is far ahead of the United States in time.

00:03:20.682 --> 00:03:23.079
When November 19 begins in Auckland,

00:03:23.079 --> 00:03:25.876
November 18 is still underway across America.

00:03:26.026 --> 00:03:27.230
No time travel.

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:28.836
No secret Rockstar invitation.

00:03:28.836 --> 00:03:33.251
Just different countries reaching the same calendar date at different moments.

00:03:33.251 --> 00:03:37.266
And that's the detail that makes this story so interesting.

00:03:37.266 --> 00:03:41.681
The game isn't officially releasing on November 18 in New Zealand.

00:03:41.681 --> 00:03:43.287
It's November 19 there.

00:03:43.287 --> 00:03:46.498
It's America that hasn't reached November 19 yet.

00:03:46.648 --> 00:03:47.003
So,

00:03:47.003 --> 00:03:48.425
if you're in America,

00:03:48.425 --> 00:03:50.912
would you try the New Zealand trick?

00:03:50.912 --> 00:03:54.821
Or would you rather wait for your own region's official unlock?

00:03:54.821 --> 00:03:56.597
Because one thing is certain.

00:03:56.597 --> 00:03:58.374
The countdown may be global.

00:03:58.374 --> 00:03:59.440
But midnight isn't.

